{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And she said, I will draw for your camels as well.</b> This mightiness in Rebekah, to draw for all his camels, was not within the realm of the possible except by divine assistance — all the more so according to the opinion of the Midrash, that she was three years old. But the matter belonged to the totality of the success that Abraham had been promised: ״He will send His angel with you and make your journey succeed.״ Therefore you will find that the great Name, which is the Name of Gevurah, is alluded to in this verse. And further know that the rule of the gimel is to be daggeshed, and an alef is inscribed in the word ותאמר. And understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:43.077865158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}